{
  "_about": "Reviewed and amended by Tomás 2026-10-08 (see flavour-rules-tomas-review.md). Original proposed 2026-10-06 (matching owner). Derives a pour's 0..1 strength per guest flavour from its authored spec ingredients. Rule = regex on the ingredient key -> base strength. Amount scaling: >=20 ml x1.0, 7.5-20 ml x0.6, smaller/dashes/drops x0.3. A pour's strength for a flavour = max over its ingredients, capped at 1. 'sweet' is not regex-based: it is the pour's sugar concentration (live dps-tools ingredient table), ranked across the collection (top third 1.0, middle 0.5). Garnish is ignored (57 pours carry a citrus peel; counting it would make 'citrusy' meaningless).",
